"Summary of earlier turns (the ticket text itself is not in the transcript I was given, so the goal is inferred from the searches).\n\nTurn 1: search for \"locked\" in apps/canvas/src. Findings relevant to the Radar \"locked card\":\n- apps/canvas/src/ops/Radar.tsx (~lines 979-1030) renders the locked card: div.radar-locked[data-testid=radar-locked], a close button (.radar-x.radar-locked-close, testid radar-locked-close, onClick setSelectedId(undefined)), .radar-locked-head with .radar-locked-title and .radar-locked-kind (flight route, or task axis), .radar-locked-facts (a .radar-locked-fact per fact with label/value), and up to three .radar-locked-actions blocks (Acknowledge, Open task, Details buttons). Line 195 has a helper naming what the card and task row lead with; line 755 releases the lock on a filter change.\n- apps/canvas/src/ops/RadarScope.tsx:145 renders the reticle (testid radar-reticle, data-locked=selected.id).\n- apps/canvas/src/ops/Radar.test.tsx has many tests on the locked card (about lines 343-530, 778-1136, 1505-1516). They expect the card text not to match /LOCKED|BEARING|RING/ and to have 2 .radar-locked-fact elements for a task, and the departure card to show 13:00 rather than BAND/BEARING.\n- i18n/messages.ts has keys ops.radar.locked, lockedMeta, lockedMetaDeparture in en/es/fr (the old \"LOCKED / BEARING / RING\" meta strings). The card no longer seems to use them in the JSX seen.\n- Other \"locked/blocked\" hits (viewerLocale, viewerZone, horizonModel, opsMenuMemory, ReplacementCandidate, Launchpad clockedRead) are unrelated storage-blocked or data-blocked code.\n\nTurn 2: read_file apps/canvas/src/ops/radar.css (the result was cut at about 20000 characters, ending around .radar-disc). Locked-card styling seen:\n- .radar-locked is declared twice: line ~103 (position: relative) and line ~133 (display:flex; row; gap 10px; padding 16px 18px; radius 12px; amber border; gradient background). A light-theme override exists near line 325.\n- .radar-locked-close is absolute at top/right 12px; .radar-locked-meta has padding-right 40px and a mono 11px style; .radar-locked-head has padding-right 36px. The facts grid is 2 columns. Buttons use .radar-primary / .radar-secondary (min-height 44px); .radar-x is a 28px circular close button.\n- Observation: .radar-locked is display:flex with flex-direction: row, while its children (close button, head, facts, detail, actions) look like they are meant to stack vertically. This could be the layout bug being investigated, but it is not confirmed.\n\nNo edits have been made yet. Next step would be to read the rest of radar.css and the Radar.tsx locked-card JSX (lines ~975-1035) to confirm and fix."
